BBUUGGSS
       As at glibc 2.8, if a thread attributes object is initialized using
       pptthhrreeaadd__aattttrr__iinniitt(3), then the scheduling policy of the attributes
       object is set to SSCCHHEEDD__OOTTHHEERR and the scheduling priority is set to 0.
       However, if the inherit‐scheduler attribute is then set to
       PPTTHHRREEAADD__EEXXPPLLIICCIITT__SSCCHHEEDD, then a thread created using the attribute
       object wrongly inherits its scheduling attributes from the creating
       thread.  This bug does not occur if either the scheduling policy or
       scheduling priority attribute is explicitly set in the thread
       attributes object before calling pptthhrreeaadd__ccrreeaattee(3).

